  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let a function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be defined as,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left left\" columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\".2em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>if</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>if</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>b</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>if</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is the greatest integer less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is continuous on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to:</p>"
  },
